          "why": "The depth byte of each combination's flanger half, read as a pitch excursion the way both single types' were. That reading is what separated the flanger's modulator from the chorus's on the types that stand alone, and it is the same question here one level down: a stage that shares a delay may still be driven by a modulator of its own. It is asked at the pre-delay the comb here was read at, so the two readings are of one configuration."
